  "inferenceRules": [
    "General-purpose Missile warhead maturation is primarily an energetic-yield question in CP116. Pure GP candidates keep SPEN/APEN fixed at the existing baseline so penetration specialization is not bundled invisibly into the GP line.",
    "Penetration-bundled GP profiles are controls, not preferred designs. Their purpose is to measure how much apparent GP strength comes from silently adding specialist SPEN/APEN.",
    "Matched-DAM SPEN-only and APEN-only GP controls isolate which penetration axis creates the apparent benefit before the combined penetration control is interpreted.",
    "Specialist warheads are generation-relative: they retain a contemporary energetic packet but trade yield and/or the opposite penetration axis for a narrow anti-Armor or anti-Shield effect.",
    "A specialist is healthy when it improves its intended niche while losing enough elsewhere that contemporary GP remains the balanced default under uncertainty.",
    "Weapon families are not expected to converge on equal performance. Kinetic, Energy, and Missile identity remains asymmetric by design.",
    "Kinetic saturation represents coverage through higher ACC on one battery attack package; smaller packets remain vulnerable to flat protection. TL8/TL9 candidates scale packet size from contemporary projectile energy instead of freezing TL6 packet values forever.",
    "Kinetic tandem packages retain one hit roll and resolve ordered internal packets. Reversed controls measure whether layer sequencing creates the niche.",
    "Controlled fixtures expose characteristic space only and are never production-promotion gates.",
    "Normal payload variants use generic magazine accounting; rare Exotic ammunition remains individually tracked outside this study.",
    "No CP116 result automatically changes CP109/CP110 values, the Concept, Storyboard TL placement, or C#/Godot production behavior."
  ],
